        "procedure": "Dy(NO3)3·6H2O (0.0114 g, 0.025 mmol) and H2L (0.0073 g, 0.025 mmol) were dissolved in a mixed solution of CH3OH (8 mL), CH2Cl2 (5 mL) and CH3CN (2 mL). Triethylamine (27 μL) was added to bring the pH close to 7. The mixture was stirred for about 2 h at room temperature, filtered, and the filtrate was kept in a programmed heating oven at 80 °C for 48 h in a 20 mL glass sample vial. After cooling to room temperature, block-shaped crystals precipitated from the mother liquor.",
